@anon.dc25e0270270115ca7d85177366aae1d.110 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [1203 x i8] }> <{ [1203 x i8] c"Data includes for wheels.\0A\0AEach entry is a directory, whose contents are copied to the matching directory in the wheel\0Ain `<name>-<version>.data/(purelib|platlib|headers|scripts|data)`. Upon installation, this\0Adata is moved to its target location, as defined by\0A<https://docs.python.org/3.12/library/sysconfig.html#installation-paths>. Usually, small\0Adata files are included by placing them in the Python module instead of using data includes.\0A\0A- `scripts`: Installed to the directory for executables, `<venv>/bin` on Unix or\0A  `<venv>\\Scripts` on Windows. This directory is added to `PATH` when the virtual\0A  environment  is activated or when using `uv run`, so this data type can be used to install\0A  additional binaries. Consider using `project.scripts` instead for Python entrypoints.\0A- `data`: Installed over the virtualenv environment root.\0A\0A    Warning: This may override existing files!\0A\0A- `headers`: Installed to the include directory. Compilers building Python packages\0A  with this package as build requirement use the include directory to find additional header\0A  files.\0A- `purelib` and `platlib`: Installed to the `site-packages` directory. It is not recommended\0A  to uses these two options." }>, align 1
